            "output": "<path>/mnt/hdd/ciya_space/work/repo/Linux_post_install/DOC/AGENT_Context_Project.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # AGENT Context — Linux_post_install Project\n2: \n3: > **Purpose:** Single-source context document so any AI agent can understand the project, navigate the codebase, and make correct contributions.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## Document Map\n8: \n9: > Auto-generated section index (line ranges). Run `make gen` to refresh.\n10: \n11: <!-- GEN:START docmap -->\n12: | ## 1. Project Overview | 28–43 |\n13: | ## 2. Directory Structure | 44–186 |\n14: | ## 3. Installation Flow | 187–239 |\n15: | ## 4. The `pos` CLI System | 240–306 |\n16: | ## 5. Shared Library — `lib/common.sh` | 307–338 |\n17: | ## 6. Docker Compose / ScaleTail | 339–381 |\n18: | ## 7. Optional Apps (`apps/`) | 382–411 |\n19: | ## 8. Entertainment Module | 412–425 |\n20: | ## 9. Systemd Services | 426–438 |\n21: | ## 10. Configuration Files | 439–465 |\n22: | ## 11. Coding Conventions | 466–498 |\n23: | ## 12. Development Workflow | 499–551 |\n24: | ## 13. Key File Quick Reference | 552–605 |\n25: | ## 14. Common Tasks for Agents | 606–631 |\n26: <!-- GEN:END docmap -->\n27: \n28: ## 1. Project Overview\n29: \n30: **Linux_post_install** is a personal bootstrap and homelab toolkit for Debian/Ubuntu. One command turns a bare install into a fully productive machine:\n31: \n32: - Automated system package installation (25+ packages)\n33: - A unified CLI (`pos`) for network, Docker, media, system, and SSH tasks\n34: - Optional desktop application installers (15 apps)\n35: - Docker Compose service management via ScaleTail templates (119+ self-hosted services with Tailscale sidecar)\n36: - Systemd service management for boot-time automation\n37: \n38: **Repository:** `https://gitea.skink-platy.ts.net/admin/Linux_post_install`\n39: **Target OS:** Debian / Ubuntu (uses `apt`)\n40: **Shell:** Bash (`#!/usr/bin/env bash`)\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 2. Directory Structure\n45: \n46: ```\n47: Linux_post_install/\n48: ├── install.sh              # Main orchestrator — entry point\n49: ├── preinstall.sh           # Phase 1: system packages via apt + yt-dlp\n50: ├── postinstall.sh          # Phase 3: PATH, bash completion, systemd services\n51: │\n52: ├── lib/\n53: │   ├── common.sh           # Shared library (colors, logging, spinner, timer, run, load_system_env)\n54: │   ├── flags.sh            # Feature flag store (flag_set/clear/is_set/value/list/status)\n55: │   ├── notify.sh           # Multi-platform alerting (notify_send) — sourced opt-in, silent-fails\n56: │   └── entertainment-lib.sh # Entertainment module lib (ENABLED list, scheduler sync)\n57: │\n58: ├── bin/                    # CLI tools — installed to /usr/local/bin/\n59: │   ├── pos                 # Main dispatcher — smart arg matching to pos-* scripts\n60: <!-- GEN:START tree -->\n61: │   ├── pos-ai-gemini                       # Chat with Google Gemini (ask, chat, models, sessions)\n62: │   ├── pos-communication-matrix-listener   # Matrix listener: map /command → bash, run them on room messages\n63: │   ├── pos-communication-matrix-sender     # Send messages to a Matrix room via the client-server API (send, test, login)\n64: │   ├── pos-communication-telegram-listener # Telegram bot listener: map /command → bash, run them on chat messages\n65: │   ├── pos-communication-telegram-sender   # Send Telegram messages/files/links/stickers via Bot API (send, test)\n66: │   ├── pos-config                          # Interactive editor for the tools' runtime config (reads # POS_CONFIG: registry)\n67: │   ├── pos-docker-compose                  # Docker Compose service manager (ls/up/down/restart/logs/update/config)\n68: │   ├── pos-docker-health                   # One-glance container health dashboard (exits 1 if unhealthy)\n69: │   ├── pos-docker-ps                       # Enhanced container overview (health, IPs, ports, uptime)\n70: │   ├── pos-docker-vbox                     # Disposable Docker-based VMs (create/enter/start/stop/rm/ls)\n71: │   ├── pos-entertainment-config            # Show or edit the entertainment config (ENABLED auto-trigger list, weather location)\n72: │   ├── pos-entertainment-disable           # Disable a plugin's auto-trigger (remove it from ENABLED)\n73: │   ├── pos-entertainment-enable            # Enable an auto-trigger for a plugin on a schedule\n74: │   ├── pos-entertainment-send              # Run a public-API plugin and send its output via Telegram (default sender)\n75: │   ├── pos-entertainment-status            # Show enabled plugins and scheduler state\n76: │   ├── pos-media-mp3                       # Download audio as MP3 (yt-dlp)\n77: │   ├── pos-media-mp4                       # Download video as MP4 (smart/interactive format select)\n78: │   ├── pos-network-checkport               # Check TCP port connectivity\n79: │   ├── pos-network-hotspot                 # Wi-Fi hotspot via create_ap + wihotspot-gui\n80: │   ├── pos-network-ip                      # Show interfaces, routes, public IP + location\n81: │   ├── pos-network-scan                    # Parallel ping sweep of CIDR\n82: │   ├── pos-ssh-load-keys                   # Load all SSH keys into the agent\n83: │   ├── pos-system-backup                   # Encrypted (AES-256) folder snapshots (tar + gpg)\n84: │   ├── pos-system-event-trigger            # State-based rule monitors; alerts via notify when a check crosses a threshold\n85: │   ├── pos-system-firewall                 # Interactive UFW management\n86: │   ├── pos-system-health                   # Host health dashboard (disk, RAM, services, backup age, fail2ban, docker); exit 1 if any FAIL\n87: │   ├── pos-system-nfs-client               # Mount NFS shares (ephemeral or persistent systemd mount units)\n88: │   ├── pos-system-nfs-server               # Manage the NFS kernel server (status, share/unshare exports, enable/disable)\n89: │   ├── pos-tree                            # Show the pos CLI command tree: categories, commands, and subcommands\n90: │   ├── pos-usb-server                      # USB Redirector server control (--ls, --share; prompts when args omitted)\n91: <!-- GEN:END tree -->\n92: │   ├── flag-reader         # Inspect feature flags (list/status/--raw)\n93: │   ├── flag-set            # Set a feature flag (optionally with a value)\n94: │   ├── flag-clear          # Unset a feature flag\n95: │   ├── wr-*                # Legacy wrappers → pos (backward compat)\n96: │   ├── mp3, mp4, vbox      # Legacy convenience wrappers → pos\n97: │   └── ssh-load-all        # Legacy wrapper → pos ssh load-keys\n98: │\n99: ├── features/               # User-customizable scripts (installed via --feature)\n100: │   └── autostart.sh        # Boot-time script (via systemd, flag-gated)\n101: │\n102: ├── entertainment/          # Public-API plugins for pos entertainment send (→ /usr/local/bin)\n103: │   ├── weather.sh          # Current weather via Open-Meteo (no API key)\n104: │   ├── joke.sh             # Random dad joke via icanhazdadjoke (no API key)\n105: │   └── gold.sh             # Gold spot (XAU/USD) via goldprice.dev (no API key)\n106: │\n107: ├── templates/              # Dev-only scaffolds — NOT installed by install.sh\n108: │   ├── pos-tool.sh         # New `pos` CLI tool (→ bin/pos-<cat>-<cmd>)\n109: │   ├── app.sh              # New optional app installer (→ apps/<cat>/<name>.sh)\n110: │   └── feature.sh          # New feature script (→ features/<name>.sh)\n111: │\n112: ├── x64_bin/                # Precompiled binaries, copied to /usr/local/bin on x86_64\n113: │   ├── create_ap           # Wi-Fi AP CLI (bash script)\n114: │   ├── wihotspot           # Wrapper → wihotspot-gui\n115: │   └── wihotspot-gui       # GTK3 hotspot GUI (x86-64 ELF)\n116: │                           # future: arm64_bin/ picked up automatically on aarch64\n117: │\n118: ├── apps/                   # Optional desktop app installers (by category)\n119: │   ├── install.sh          # Interactive picker / orchestrator\n120: │   ├── browsers/\n121: │   │   └── brave.sh       # Brave Browser (APT repo)\n122: │   ├── development/\n123: │   │   ├── opencode.sh    # opencode AI agent (official script)\n124: │   │   └── vscode.sh      # VS Code (Microsoft APT repo)\n125: │   ├── media/\n126: │   │   ├── obs.sh         # OBS Studio (apt)\n127: │   │   ├── scrcpy.sh      # scrcpy Android mirror (GitHub release)\n128: │   │   └── vlc.sh         # VLC media player (apt)\n129: │   ├── networking/\n130: │   │   ├── netbird.sh     # NetBird VPN (official script)\n131: │   │   ├── tailscale.sh   # Tailscale VPN (official script)\n132: │   │   └── zerotier.sh    # ZeroTier VPN (official script)\n133: │   ├── remote-access/\n134: │   │   ├── termius.sh     # Termius SSH client (.deb)\n135: │   │   └── vnc-viewer.sh  # TigerVNC Viewer (apt)\n136: │   ├── system/\n137: │   │   ├── docker.sh      # Docker Engine (get.docker.com)\n138: │   │   └── qemu.sh        # QEMU + libvirt + KVM (apt)\n139: │   └── utilities/\n140: │       ├── affine.sh      # AFFiNE knowledge base (AppImage)\n141: │       ├── btop.sh        # btop resource monitor (apt)\n142: │       ├── localsend.sh   # LocalSend (flatpak)\n143: │       └── tsui.sh        # Tailscale config TUI (official install script)\n144: │\n145: ├── completions/\n146: │   └── pos.bash            # Bash tab-completion for the pos CLI\n147: │\n148: ├── config/\n149: │   ├── authorized_keys     # SSH public keys (gitignored)\n150: │   ├── entertainment.env   # Weather location template (auto-installed by postinstall)\n151: │   └── ai.env              # Gemini API key + model template (auto-installed by postinstall)\n152: │\n153: ├── compose/\n154: │   └── scale-tail/         # Git submodule → ScaleTail templates (119+ services)\n155: │\n156: ├── systemd/\n157: │   ├── autostart.service   # Runs autostart.sh on boot\n158: │   ├── ssh-agent.service   # System-wide SSH agent socket\n159: │   ├── pos-health.service  # Runs the health digest as the installing user (triggered by timer)\n160: │   └── pos-health.timer    # Daily 08:00 trigger for the health digest (enabled when Telegram is configured)\n161: │\n162: ├── scripts/                # Dev tooling\n163: │   ├── gen-docs.sh         # Regenerates code-derived doc sections + completion flags\n164: │   ├── check-sync.sh       # `make check` gate (syntax, exec bits, doc/code sync, smoke)\n165: │   └── install-hooks.sh    # Installs the opt-in pre-commit hook (`make hook`)\n166: │\n167: ├── README.md               # User-facing intro + quick start (links into DOC/)\n168: │\n169: ├── DOC/                    # All documentation\n170: │   ├── README.md           # Docs index\n171: │   ├── SCRIPTS.md          # Installer scripts, libs, features — reference\n172: │   ├── POS.md              # pos CLI reference\n173: │   ├── APPS.md             # Optional apps reference\n174: │   ├── SYSTEMD.md          # Systemd units + completion\n175: │   ├── DEV.md              # Developer guide\n176: │   ├── HOWTO.md            # Hands-on guides index (per-category tutorials)\n177: │   ├── howto/              # Per-category tutorials (network, docker, media, system, ssh, usb, communication, entertainment)\n178: │   ├── AGENT_Context_Project.md  # This file — AI agent context\n179: │   └── algorithm.md        # Algorithm diagrams\n180: │\n181: ├── .gitignore              # Excludes secrets, Python artifacts, OS files\n182: └── .gitmodules             # Submodule: compose/scale-tail → ScaleTail\n183: ```\n184: \n185: ---\n186: \n187: ## 3. Installation Flow\n188: \n189: ```\n190: User runs: ./install.sh [--apps|--full|--feature|--dry-run|--skip <phase>|--steps <spec>]\n191: │\n192: ├─ Phase 1: preinstall.sh        (requires root)\n193: │   └─ apt update + installs 25+ packages + yt-dlp + fail2ban\n194: │\n195: ├─ Phase 2: install.sh           (requires root)\n196: │   └─ Copies bin/* → /usr/local/bin/ (chmod 755)\n197: │   └─ Copies lib/common.sh + lib/flags.sh + lib/notify.sh + lib/entertainment-lib.sh → /usr/local/bin/ (chmod 644)\n198: │   └─ Copies x64_bin/* → /usr/local/bin/ on x86_64 (arm64_bin/ on aarch64)\n199: │   └─ [if --feature] Copies features/* → /usr/local/bin/ (asks before overwriting),\n200: │                      then sets the matching feature flag\n201: │\n202: ├─ Phase 3: postinstall.sh       (runs as user)\n203: │   └─ Configures fail2ban (SSH jail: 5 retries, 1h ban)\n204: │   └─ PATH export in ~/.bashrc\n205: │   └─ Bash completion for pos CLI\n206: │   └─ Copies systemd/*.service + systemd/*.timer → /etc/systemd/system/, enables them\n207: │      (autostart.service only when the `autostart` flag is set;\n208: │       pos-health.timer only when the user's Telegram config exists)\n209: │\n210: ├─ Phase 4: ScaleTail clone\n211: │   └─ Shallow-clones ScaleTail templates to /usr/local/share/linux_post_install/scale-tail\n212: │\n213: └─ [if --apps or --full]: apps/install.sh\n214:     └─ Interactive picker (or --all for non-interactive)\n215: ```\n216: \n217: **After install, the repo can be deleted** — all tools live in `/usr/local/bin/` and templates in `/usr/local/share/linux_post_install/`.\n218: \n219: ### install.sh Flags\n220: \n221: | Flag | Purpose |\n222: |------|---------|\n223: | `--apps` | Run interactive app picker after core install |\n224: | `--full` | Core install + all apps (non-interactive) |\n225: | `--feature` | Install `features/` scripts to `/usr/local/bin/` (asks before overwriting), set their flags |\n226: | `--dry-run` | Preview without executing |\n227: | `--skip <phase>` | Skip a phase (repeatable): `preinstall`, `scripts`, `postinstall`, `scalepoint`, `apps` |\n228: | `--steps <spec>` | Run only specific phases. Format: `1,3,4` or `1-3` |\n229: | `--no-color` | Disable colored output |\n230: \n231: ### pos Output Logging\n232: \n233: All non-interactive `pos` commands log output to `~/.local/share/linux_post_install/logs/`:\n234: - Per-command files: `YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_pos_<cmd>.log` (full stdout+stderr)\n235: - Main log: `pos.log` (command + timestamp + exit code for every invocation)\n236: - Interactive commands (`system-firewall`, `media-mp4`) only log invocation, not output\n237: \n238: ---\n239: \n240: ## 4. The `pos` CLI System\n241: \n242: ### How It Works\n243: \n244: `bin/pos` is the main dispatcher. It:\n245: 1. Scans its own directory for all executable `pos-*` files\n246: 2. Extracts category-subcommand names from filenames\n247: 3. Uses variable-length argument matching to find the right script\n248: \n249: **Example:** `pos docker compose up jellyfin`\n250: - Tries `pos-docker-compose-up-jellyfin` (not found)\n251: - Tries `pos-docker-compose-up` (not found)\n252: - Finds `pos-docker-compose` (runs with args `up jellyfin`)\n253: \n254: ### Available Commands\n255: \n256: | Category | Command | Script | Description |\n257: |----------|---------|--------|-------------|\n258: <!-- GEN:START dispatch -->\n259: | ai | gemini | `pos-ai-gemini` | Chat with Google Gemini (ask, chat, models, sessions) |\n260: | communication | matrix-listener | `pos-communication-matrix-listener` | Matrix listener: map /command → bash, run them on room messages |\n261: | communication | matrix-sender | `pos-communication-matrix-sender` | Send messages to a Matrix room via the client-server API (send, test, login) |\n262: | communication | telegram-listener | `pos-communication-telegram-listener` | Telegram bot listener: map /command → bash, run them on chat messages |\n263: | communication | telegram-sender | `pos-communication-telegram-sender` | Send Telegram messages/files/links/stickers via Bot API (send, test) |\n264: |  | config | `pos-config` | Interactive editor for the tools' runtime config (reads # POS_CONFIG: registry) |\n265: | docker | compose | `pos-docker-compose` | Docker Compose service manager (ls/up/down/restart/logs/update/config) |\n266: | docker | health | `pos-docker-health` | One-glance container health dashboard (exits 1 if unhealthy) |\n267: | docker | ps | `pos-docker-ps` | Enhanced container overview (health, IPs, ports, uptime) |\n268: | docker | vbox | `pos-docker-vbox` | Disposable Docker-based VMs (create/enter/start/stop/rm/ls) |\n269: | entertainment | config | `pos-entertainment-config` | Show or edit the entertainment config (ENABLED auto-trigger list, weather location) |\n270: | entertainment | disable | `pos-entertainment-disable` | Disable a plugin's auto-trigger (remove it from ENABLED) |\n271: | entertainment | enable | `pos-entertainment-enable` | Enable an auto-trigger for a plugin on a schedule |\n272: | entertainment | send | `pos-entertainment-send` | Run a public-API plugin and send its output via Telegram (default sender) |\n273: | entertainment | status | `pos-entertainment-status` | Show enabled plugins and scheduler state |\n274: | media | mp3 | `pos-media-mp3` | Download audio as MP3 (yt-dlp) |\n275: | media | mp4 | `pos-media-mp4` | Download video as MP4 (smart/interactive format select) |\n276: | network | checkport | `pos-network-checkport` | Check TCP port connectivity |\n277: | network | hotspot | `pos-network-hotspot` | Wi-Fi hotspot via create_ap + wihotspot-gui |\n278: | network | ip | `pos-network-ip` | Show interfaces, routes, public IP + location |\n279: | network | scan | `pos-network-scan` | Parallel ping sweep of CIDR |\n280: | ssh | load-keys | `pos-ssh-load-keys` | Load all SSH keys into the agent |\n281: | system | backup | `pos-system-backup` | Encrypted (AES-256) folder snapshots (tar + gpg) |\n282: | system | event-trigger | `pos-system-event-trigger` | State-based rule monitors; alerts via notify when a check crosses a threshold |\n283: | system | firewall | `pos-system-firewall` | Interactive UFW management |\n284: | system | health | `pos-system-health` | Host health dashboard (disk, RAM, services, backup age, fail2ban, docker); exit 1 if any FAIL |\n285: | system | nfs-client | `pos-system-nfs-client` | Mount NFS shares (ephemeral or persistent systemd mount units) |\n286: | system | nfs-server | `pos-system-nfs-server` | Manage the NFS kernel server (status, share/unshare exports, enable/disable) |\n287: |  | tree | `pos-tree` | Show the pos CLI command tree: categories, commands, and subcommands |\n288: | usb | server | `pos-usb-server` | USB Redirector server control (--ls, --share; prompts when args omitted) |\n289: <!-- GEN:END dispatch -->\n290: \n291: ### Legacy Wrappers\n292: \n293: These forward to `pos` transparently: `wr-ip`, `wr-checkport`, `wr-scan-ping`, `wr-docker`, `wr-compose`, `wr-ufw`, `mp3`, `mp4`, `vbox`, `ssh-load-all`.\n294: \n295: ### pos docker vbox Details\n296: \n297: `pos-docker-vbox` manages disposable Docker containers as lightweight VMs:\n298: \n299: - **Container labeling:** All created containers get `linux_post_install.vbox=true` label\n300: - **`ls` filtering:** `docker ps --filter label=linux_post_install.vbox=true` — only shows vbox-managed containers\n301: - **Post-create prompt:** After `create`, asks \"Enter now? [Y/n]\" using `confirm` helper\n302: - **Working dir detection:** `enter` auto-detects bind mount path from container labels\n303: - **Custom dirs:** `--dir <path>` or `--dir .` for current directory\n304: \n305: ---\n306: \n307: ## 5. Shared Library — `lib/common.sh`\n308: \n309: Sourced by most scripts. Provides:\n310: \n311: | Function | Purpose |\n312: |----------|---------|\n313: | `log \"msg\"` | Green `[+]` status message |\n314: | `warn \"msg\"` | Yellow `[!]` warning |\n315: | `err \"msg\"` | Red `ERROR:` + exit 1 |\n316: | `ok \"msg\"` | Green `OK` prefix |\n317: | `section \"title\"` | Cyan-bordered section header |\n318: | `step N T \"msg\"` | Numbered step header (e.g., `[1/4] Installing`) |\n319: | `run cmd` | Executes command, respects `$DRY_RUN` |\n320: | `spawn \"msg\" cmd` | Runs with animated braille spinner, elapsed time, OK/FAIL status; respects `$DRY_RUN` |\n321: | `timer_start` / `timer_stop` | Elapsed time tracking |\n322: | `confirm \"prompt\" [default]` | y/N or Y/n prompt |\n323: | `load_system_env` | Loads `~/.config/linux_post_install/system.env` (env already exported wins) |\n324: \n325: **Auto-detects TTY** — disables colors when piped.\n326: \n327: **Source pattern:**\n328: ```bash\n329: source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../lib/common.sh\"\n330: ```\n331: \n332: **Scripts that do NOT source common.sh** (self-contained):\n333: <!-- GEN:START selfcontained -->\n334: `pos`, `pos-communication-matrix-listener`, `pos-communication-matrix-sender`, `pos-communication-telegram-listener`, `pos-communication-telegram-sender`, `pos-network-checkport`, `pos-network-hotspot`, `pos-network-ip`, `pos-network-scan`, `pos-ssh-load-keys`, `pos-system-firewall`.\n335: <!-- GEN:END selfcontained -->\n336: \n337: ---\n338: \n339: ## 6. Docker Compose / ScaleTail\n340: \n341: ### Architecture\n342: \n343: ScaleTail provides 119+ Docker Compose templates with a Tailscale sidecar pattern (`network_mode: service:tailscale`). Each service gets a `tail-xxxxx.ts.net` URL with optional automatic HTTPS.\n344: \n345: ```\n346: /usr/local/share/linux_post_install/scale-tail/    # Templates (git repo)\n347: └── services/<name>/\n348:     ├── compose.yaml\n349:     └── .env\n350: \n351: ~/.config/linux_post_install/compose.env           # Global defaults (TS_AUTHKEY, TZ, DNS_SERVER, SERVICES_BASE)\n352: \n353: /srv/<service>/                         # Active deployments (default base)\n354:     ├── compose.yaml                    # From template (refreshed on update)\n355:     ├── .env                            # User config (preserved across updates)\n356:     ├── config/\n357:     └── data/\n358: ```\n359: \n360: ### Key Commands\n361: \n362: | Command | Description |\n363: |---------|-------------|\n364: | `pos docker compose ls` | List all available ScaleTail services |\n365: | `pos docker compose up <svc>` | Deploy service to SERVICES_BASE |\n366: | `pos docker compose down <svc>` | Stop a deployed service |\n367: | `pos docker compose restart <svc>` | Restart a service |\n368: | `pos docker compose logs <svc> [-f]` | View/follow logs |\n369: | `pos docker compose update` | Pull latest templates, refresh compose.yaml (preserves .env) |\n370: | `pos docker compose config set K=V` | Set global config value |\n371: | `pos docker compose config show` | Display current config |\n372: \n373: ### Global Config Keys\n374: \n375: - `TS_AUTHKEY` — Tailscale auth key (required)\n376: - `TZ` — Timezone\n377: - `DNS_SERVER` — Custom DNS\n378: - `SERVICES_BASE` — Deployment root (default: `/srv`)\n379: \n380: ---\n381: \n382: ## 7. Optional Apps (`apps/`)\n383: \n384: ### How They Work\n385: \n386: - `apps/install.sh` auto-discovers all `apps/<category>/*.sh` files (excluding itself)\n387: - Three modes: interactive (default), `--all`, or specific app names as arguments\n388: - `--uninstall` switches to uninstall mode (same selection, invokes app scripts with `uninstall` argument)\n389: - Interactive TUI groups apps by category with section headers\n390: - Each app script is standalone, idempotent, sources `lib/common.sh`\n391: - Every app script defines `install_<name>()` **and** `uninstall_<name>()`, dispatched via `case \"${1:-}\" in uninstall) ...`\n392: \n393: ### Installation Methods\n394: \n395: | Method | Apps |\n396: |--------|------|\n397: | `apt install` | btop, obs, vlc, vnc-viewer, qemu |\n398: | APT repo (GPG + repo) | brave, vscode |\n399: | Official `curl \\| sh` | docker, tailscale, netbird, zerotier, opencode |\n400: | AppImage | affine |\n401: | GitHub release binary | scrcpy |\n402: | Flatpak | localsend |\n403: | .deb package | termius |\n404: \n405: ### Adding a New App\n406: \n407: 1. Create `apps/<category>/<name>.sh` following the template in DOC/DEV.md\n408: 2. It auto-appears in the interactive picker — no registration needed\n409: \n410: ---\n411: \n412: ## 8. Entertainment Module\n413: \n414: Public-API \"entertainment\" plugins (weather, joke, gold) that can auto-send their output to Telegram on a schedule.\n415: \n416: - **CLI:** `pos entertainment {config|enable|disable|send|status}` — see the dispatch table in §4 and POS.md [entertainment](#entertainment).\n417: - **Library:** `lib/entertainment-lib.sh` — config-file helpers, ENABLED-list parsing, plugin lookup, and scheduler sync (systemd user timers, crontab fallback).\n418: - **Plugins:** `entertainment/*.sh` — standalone scripts that fetch a public API and **print the message to stdout** (what gets sent). Each declares its name with a `# POS_PLUGIN: <name>` header; a new plugin is auto-discovered.\n419: - **Config:** `~/.config/linux_post_install/entertainment.env` (ENABLED auto-trigger list, weather location). Template: `config/entertainment.env`, auto-installed by postinstall.\n420: - **Sending:** `pos entertainment send <plugin> [--print] [--markdown]` runs the plugin and delivers via `pos communication telegram sender send`.\n421: - **Auto-trigger:** `pos entertainment enable <plugin> <interval>` writes the plugin into ENABLED and syncs a systemd user timer (allowed intervals: `5m 10m 15m 30m 45m hourly 2h 6h 12h daily weekly`, or `OnCalendar=…`); `disable` removes it.\n422: - **Docs:** DEV.md \"Adding an Entertainment Plugin\" (§1 step list) and POS.md [entertainment](#entertainment).\n423: \n424: ---\n425: \n426: ## 9. Systemd Services\n427: \n428: | Service | File | Purpose |\n429: |---------|------|---------|\n430: | `ssh-agent.service` | `systemd/ssh-agent.service` | System-wide SSH agent, socket at `/run/ssh-agent/socket` |\n431: | `autostart.service` | `systemd/autostart.service` | Runs `autostart.sh` on boot |\n432: | `pos-health.service` | `systemd/pos-health.service` | Runs `pos system health --send --markdown` once (oneshot) as the installing user |\n433: | `pos-health.timer` | `systemd/pos-health.timer` | Daily 08:00 trigger for the digest (enabled only when `~/.config/linux_post_install/telegram.env` exists) |\n434: \n435: All `.service` files in `systemd/` are automatically copied to `/etc/systemd/system/` and enabled by `postinstall.sh` (timers too, when present).\n436: \n437: ---\n438: \n439: ## 10. Configuration Files\n440: \n441: ### Gitignored Secrets\n442: \n443: - `config/rclone.conf` — rclone remote config (OAuth tokens)\n444: - `config/authorized_keys` — SSH public keys\n445: \n446: ### Runtime Config\n447: \n448: - `~/.config/linux_post_install/compose.env` — Docker Compose global defaults\n449: - `~/.config/linux_post_install/entertainment.env` — entertainment plugin defaults: weather location + `ENABLED` auto-trigger list (`plugin, interval` pairs scheduled via `pos entertainment enable/disable`, systemd user timers); auto-installed from `config/entertainment.env` by `postinstall.sh` (no clobber, template printed)\n450: - `~/.config/linux_post_install/system.env` — shared \"system\" tool settings (loaded by `pos system health` / `pos system backup` via `load_system_env()` in `lib/common.sh`; env already exported wins over the file); template `config/system.env`\n451: - `~/.config/linux_post_install/notify.env` — alerting platform selection (`NOTIFY_PLATFORM=telegram,matrix`, comma-separated = fan out); read by `lib/notify.sh`; template `config/notify.env`\n452: - `~/.config/linux_post_install/ai.env` — Google Gemini config (`AI_GEMINI_API_KEY` secret, `AI_GEMINI_MODEL` default `gemini-2.5-flash`); read by `pos ai gemini`; template `config/ai.env`, auto-installed by postinstall, edit with `pos config ai`\n453: - `~/.bashrc` — Modified by postinstall (PATH, bash completion)\n454: \n455: ### Feature Flags\n456: \n457: System-wide flag store at `/usr/local/share/linux_post_install/flags/`:\n458: - One file per flag; **presence = set**, **file content = optional value** (dir 755, files 644).\n459: - Library: `lib/flags.sh` (installed as `/usr/local/bin/flags.sh`) — `flag_set <name> [value]`, `flag_clear <name>`, `flag_is_set <name>`, `flag_value <name>`, `flag_list`, `flag_status <name>`.\n460: - CLI: `flag-reader` (list / status / `--raw`), `flag-set`, `flag-clear`.\n461: - Set by `./install.sh --feature`; read by `postinstall.sh` to gate systemd enablement (e.g. `autostart.service` requires the `autostart` flag).\n462: - Writes use `run` + `sudo`, so they respect `--dry-run`. `FLAGS_DIR` is env-overridable for tests.\n463: \n464: ---\n465: \n466: ## 11. Coding Conventions\n467: \n468: ### Script Standards\n469: \n470: - **Shebang:** `#!/usr/bin/env bash`\n471: - **Strict mode:** `set -euo pipefail`\n472: - **Help:** Every script accepts `-h`/`--help` via `case` pattern\n473: - **Idempotency:** Check existence before creating/modifying\n474: - **Exit codes:** 0 = success, 1 = error\n475: \n476: ### Naming Conventions\n477: \n478: - `pos-<category>-<command>` — canonical tool names\n479: - `wr-*` — legacy wrappers\n480: - `apps/<category>/<name>.sh` — optional app installers\n481: - Hyphens for word separation, lowercase always\n482: \n483: ### Error Handling\n484: \n485: - `command -v <tool> &>/dev/null` to check tool availability\n486: - `set -euo pipefail` for fail-fast\n487: - `err()` for fatal errors, `warn()` for non-fatal\n488: - Confirmation prompts for destructive actions\n489: \n490: ### Security\n491: \n492: - Never hardcode secrets in scripts\n493: - Use `chmod 600` for sensitive files\n494: - Validate user input before shell commands\n495: - Use `sudo` only where necessary\n496: \n497: ---\n498: \n499: ## 12. Development Workflow\n500: \n501: ### Adding a New Feature\n502: \n503: 1. Create `features/<name>.sh` from `templates/feature.sh` (installed on demand via `./install.sh --feature`; never overwritten without asking)\n504: 2. `install.sh` auto-discovers it and sets its flag — no registration needed\n505: 3. If a systemd service depends on it, gate the service on `flag_is_set <name>` in `postinstall.sh`\n506: 4. Update `DOC/AGENT_Context_Project.md` file table if line counts change\n507: \n508: ### Adding a New App\n509: \n510: 1. Create `apps/<category>/<name>.sh` from `templates/app.sh` (per DOC/DEV.md)\n511: 2. It auto-appears in the interactive picker — no registration needed\n512: 3. Update `DOC/APPS.md` catalog table (name, category, purpose, install method)\n513: 4. Test: `bash -n apps/<cat>/<name>.sh && shellcheck apps/<cat>/<name>.sh`\n514: \n515: ### Adding a New Tool\n516: \n517: 0. Define the exact CLI verb (`pos <category> <command> [<subcommand>]`) and its runtime context before writing code: a **dev/repo-only** tool (e.g. reads repo files, like `pos tree`) or a **runtime** tool that must work from `/usr/local/bin` after the repo is deleted. Category-less `bin/pos-<cmd>` is for dispatcher/dev-level commands that fit no category (`pos-config`, `pos-tree`); everything else goes in a category.\n518: 1. Create `bin/pos-<category>-<command>` (or `bin/pos-<cmd>` for category-less) from `templates/pos-tool.sh` — must be executable (`100755`); it auto-appears in `pos <category> --help` (filename-derived, no registration)\n519: 2. Add the `# POS: <cat> <cmd> — <one-line description>` header right after the shebang (plus `# POS_FLAGS: ...` for flag-style tools and `# POS_SUBCMDS: ...` for multi-command tools) — this is the single source of truth for the generated docs; nested tools (`pos-<cat>-<a>-<b>`) auto-list under their parent tool\n520: 3. Add to `INTERACTIVE_CMDS` in `bin/pos` if it reads stdin\n521: 4. Add system deps to `PACKAGES` array in `preinstall.sh` (if needed); non-apt/manual installers → `command -v` guard in the tool instead\n522: 5. Add config logic to `postinstall.sh` (if needed, with `.gitignore` for secrets); runtime tool config → `~/.config/linux_post_install/<tool>.env` (600)\n523: 6. Update docs: `DOC/POS.md` (section table + detail — hand-written); `DOC/AGENT_Context_Project.md` generated sections (bin tree, dispatch table, self-contained list, line-count table) and completion flags update via `make gen` — never hand-edit between `GEN:START`/`GEN:END` markers; root `README.md` only if the category list changes\n524: 7. Test: `make gen && make check` — `make check` (bash -n + doc/code sync + smoke) is the definition of done; also `bin/pos help <full command> && bin/pos <category> --help`\n525: \n526: ### Testing\n527: \n528: ```bash\n529: # Syntax check all scripts\n530: for f in bin/* apps/*/*.sh lib/common.sh install.sh preinstall.sh postinstall.sh; do\n531:     bash -n \"$f\" || echo \"FAIL: $f\"\n532: done\n533: \n534: # ShellCheck linting\n535: shellcheck bin/my-script\n536: \n537: # Test in Docker\n538: docker run --rm -it -v $PWD:/repo ubuntu:22.04 bash\n539: # inside: cd /repo && ./install.sh\n540: \n541: # Test apps interactively\n542: ./apps/install.sh --all\n543: ./apps/install.sh docker vscode\n544: ```\n545: \n546: ### Commit Conventions\n547: \n548: Use conventional prefixes: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`\n549: \n550: ---\n551: \n552: ## 13. Key File Quick Reference\n553: \n554: | File | Lines | Purpose |\n555: |------|-------|---------|\n556: | `install.sh` | 206 | Main orchestrator — 4 phases with CLI flags, `--feature`, prebuilt arch bins |\n557: | `preinstall.sh` | 55 | System packages + hotspot deps + yt-dlp + fail2ban |\n558: | `postinstall.sh` | 152 | fail2ban config, PATH, bash completion, systemd (flag-gated) |\n559: | `lib/common.sh` | 144 | Shared library (log/warn/err/run/spawn, dry-run aware, `load_system_env`) |\n560: | `lib/flags.sh` | 60 | Feature flag store (set/clear/is_set/value/list/status) |\n561: | `lib/notify.sh` | 76 | Multi-platform alerting (`notify_send`) — opt-in source, silent-fails |\n562: | `lib/entertainment-lib.sh` | 350 | Entertainment module lib (ENABLED parsing, scheduler sync) |\n563: | `lib/eventer-lib.sh` | 312 | Eventer lib (rule parsing, float compare, per-rule state, user-timer sync) |\n564: | `bin/flag-reader` | 58 | Inspect flags (list/status/`--raw`) |\n565: | `bin/flag-set` | 21 | Set a flag (optionally with a value) |\n566: | `bin/flag-clear` 