he harness would continue printing. The output stopped right after \"== watch (complete on first poll) ==\". So $TOOL watch hung.\n\nHmm — why would watch hang? tellStatus with raw gid → curl stub: `method=$(printf '%s' \"$body\" | jq -r '.method')` → jq parse error on invalid JSON → method empty → `case \"\" in ... *) echo unknown method; exit 1`. So curl exits 1 → rpc: `body=$(curl ... ) || err` → err \"RPC failed\" → exit. NOT a hang.\n\nUnless — jq PARSE ERROR → jq prints error to stderr and exits nonzero... `$(...)` captures stdout only. method=\"\". Then case `*)` → echo + exit 1. curl stub exits 1. rpc errs. So watch should exit 1 quickly.\n\nHmm, so why the hang?? Unless... the `2>/dev/null || true` in watch's jq — `row=$(rpc aria2.tellStatus \"$gid\" | jq -r '...' 2>/dev/null || true)` — rpc errs → err exits 1 → the pipeline... in command substitution with `|| true` — err's exit 1 triggers `|| true` → row=\"\" → st=\"\" → no case match → `sleep 2` → LOOP FOREVER!!! THAT's the hang!\n\nBecause `rpc` calls `err` which calls `exit 1` — inside `$(rpc ... | jq ... || true)`, the exit 1 of rpc is swallowed by `|| true`. So when the daemon/curl fails, watch loops forever. Even with valid RPC it wouldn't happen, but with invalid JSON gid → curl stub exit 1 → err → `|| true` swallows → infinite loop.\n\nFix: in watch, don't swallow rpc failure. Remove `|| true` and instead let rpc's err propagate (exit). But jq failure on row extraction should be tolerated. Restructure:\n\n```bash\nlocal raw\nraw=$(rpc aria2.tellStatus \"$(json_str \"$gid\")\")\nlocal row st\nrow=$(printf '%s' \"$raw\" | jq -r '...' 2>/dev/null || true)\n```\n\nrpc failure → err exits → whole tool exits. jq failure → row=\"\" → keep polling. That's the right structure. But also — if row is empty, we keep polling forever silently. Better: when row empty → print something? Edge case; keep polling is fine (progress continues). Actually if jq fails repeatedly something's wrong; but let's keep simple: tolerate.\n\nAlso apply same for the watch-all branch: `act=$(rpc aria2.tellActive)` — rpc failure exits; fine.\n\nAnd the `st` empty → no case match → sleep → loop — with valid RPC, tellStatus always returns status. OK.\n\nNow the list rc=141 mystery. Let me run list directly with trace.",
