ouble check: does the tool install units to USER_SYSTEMD_DIR seam — yes, USER_SYSTEMD_DIR exists for the daemon unit; reuse for timer/service units.\n\nAlso the healer service ExecStart must call the tool — after install it's /usr/local/bin/pos-network-download. Use that path with fallback? The unit is written at install time on the target machine; /usr/local/bin is where postinstall puts tools. telegram-listener unit — let me check how it references itself. I'll verify during implementation (grep pos-communication-telegram-listener.service usage). For the plan I'll note \"match the listener unit's ExecStart pattern\".\n\nOne more: `retry all` in timer mode must not auto-start the daemon if it's stopped (ensure_daemon would start aria2c just to check). Guard: if daemon not active → skip entirely (exit quiet). Only heal when daemon is running. Also `ensure_healer` enable only alongside a running daemon.\n\nAlso the daemon itself: `Restart=on-failure` already. Fine.\n\nEdge: multiple errored gids from a multi-hour outage; `retry all` with net down (timer mode) does nothing each run; when net returns, first run retries all. Since addUri for many at once — fine.\n\nWhat about `watch` no-gid mode (all downloads)? On error there — currently exits \"no active downloads\" when none active. Keep as-is; auto-heal is for gid mode. Fine.\n\nNow also reconsider user's phrase: \"make sure is systemd disable after all downloding done, and enable --now when start any download\". Yes — that's the timer lifecycle. I'll make the enable point also `start`? If daemon starts with no downloads, don't enable timer (nothing to heal). Only enable when enqueueing. And `ensure_healer` should be called by add/torrent/metalink/restart/retry(interactive) — good.\n\nAlright — also potential concern: the healer service running `pos network download retry all --once --quiet` — \"quiet\" must suppress the \"no internet\" message but keep failure info? For timer runs, suppress non-essential output; th