              "patch": "Index: temp_TODO.md\n===================================================================\n--- temp_TODO.md\t\n+++ temp_TODO.md\t\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+# temp_TODO — active plan (survives context compaction)\n+\n+Standing rule: plans live in this file until the work is committed, then the file is deleted (last todo item).\n+\n+## Feature: pos network download — restart + smart retry + systemd healer\n+\n+Approved 2026-08-12. Goal: re-download from history, and make plain `pos network download add <link>` resilient to long internet outages.\n+\n+### aria2 background\n+aria2 has only `--max-tries` (5) / `--retry-wait` (0) — short immediate retries; after that a download lands in STOPPED/`error`. No long-term retry. So we build one.\n+\n+### Primitives\n+- `net_up()` — probe via seam `NET_PROBE` (default `timeout 3 bash -c '</dev/tcp/8.8.8.8/53'`; ICMP-independent). Run via `bash -c \"$NET_PROBE\"`.\n+- `resolve_gid()` — full 16-hex gid or unique 8-char prefix (tellStopped/tellActive/tellWaiting). History note: lost on daemon restart.\n+- `do_restart <gid> <dir> <seed> <split>` — internal, prints new gids (one per line).\n+- `ensure_healer()` / `healer_done()` — timer lifecycle.\n+\n+### 1. `restart <gid> [--dir --seed --split --tmux]`\n+- Torrent: rebuild magnet `magnet:?xt=urn:btih:<hash>` + `&tr=` from announceList → `aria2.addUri`.\n+- HTTP: per-file `addUri` with original `dir`/`out` (`--continue=true` resumes partial files; complete file on disk re-verifies instantly).\n+- active → err; unknown/purged → err; no usable URIs → err.\n+\n+### 2. `retry <gid|all> [--interval N=30] [--max-wait N=0=forever] [--once] [--quiet] [--dir --seed --split --tmux]`\n+- Net down: interactive waits/polls, restarts when back; `--once` (timer mode) exits quietly, next run retries.\n+- Net up: `do_restart`, then `retry_verify` polls the new gid: active/complete → ok; fast errorCode 3 → real problem (report + mark permanent, exit 1); other errors → a few checks then diagnose.\n+- Permanent-failure memory: `$CONFIG_DIR/download.retry` (id = `bt:<infohash>` or `url:<uri>`); `retry all` skips marked sources; manual restart overrides.\n+- Daemon down: interactive → err; quiet → rc 0.\n+\n+### 3. Systemd healer (lifecycle per user: enable --now on download start, disable when all done)\n+- `pos-aria2-retry.service` — Type=oneshot, `ExecStart=$runner retry all --once --quiet` (runner = /usr/local/bin w/ repo fallback + warn, listener pattern), `Environment=PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin`.\n+- `pos-aria2-retry.timer` — `OnUnitActiveSec=2min`, `Persistent=true`, `WantedBy=timers.target`.\n+- `ensure_healer` (enable --now) on add/torrent/metalink/restart/interactive-retry; `healer_done()` in retry when no active/waiting/error-stopped remain → disable.\n+\n+### 4. `watch <gid>` auto-heal\n+- status error: net up → report real error, exit 1. net down → \"network down — waiting\", poll, when back `do_restart`, switch gid, continue. Works under `--tmux`.\n+\n+### Files\n+- `bin/pos-network-download` — primitives + cmd_restart + cmd_retry + watch heal + usage + `# POS_SUBCMDS:` (20: +restart retry).\n+- Docs: `DOC/POS.md` detail rows (restart/retry/healer), `DOC/howto/network.md` outage recipe, `DOC/SYSTEMD.md` units, `AGENT_TODO.md` Done.\n+- `make gen` (completions + AGENT_Context tables) && `make check`.\n+- Tests: `/tmp/opencode/dl-test` — stub curl tellStatus fixtures (http w/ uris, torrent, active, error 3), systemctl stub enable/disable logging, NET_PROBE file-flip, new cases.\n+\n+### Verify\n+`make gen && make check` green; full stub suite green; commit `feat:`; then delete this file.\n+\n+## Todo\n+- [ ] write plan file (this)\n+- [ ] implement primitives + cmd_restart in tool\n+- [ ] implement cmd_retry + permanent state\n+- [ ] healer units + ensure_healer/healer_done\n+- [ ] watch auto-heal\n+- [ ] usage/POS_SUBCMDS/header updates\n+- [ ] extend stub harness + new test cases; suite green\n+- [ ] make gen && make check\n+- 