elink`), and whether `list` should also show markers. Let me present the plan with a recommended choice and one or two small questions.\n\nActually — the user's phrasing: \"when inserting a new link it should resume\" — they might mean: in `status`/`list` the dead download is shown, and they want to type a command with the new link. My `replace <gid> <url>` does exactly that. Good.\n\nLet me also decide the flag for \"verify the new link\" — retry_verify sleeps RETRY_VERIFY_SLEEP (default 3s, harness 1s) × up to 5. Interactive replace taking ~3s is fine (mirrors retry).\n\nLet me write the plan now. Keep it structured and concise. I'll ask 2 quick questions: command name (recommend `replace`), and whether the advisory should also appear in `list`. Actually the system says ask clarifying questions when weighing tradeoffs. I'll include the questions at the end.\n\nPlan structure:\n1. Goal\n2. Design decisions (with recommendation)\n3. Implementation steps (tool)\n4. Tests\n5. Docs + regen\n6. Open questions\n\nLet me present it.",
