ith fresh link (resumes partial file)\"`\n   - `retry_unmark \"url:$old_uri\"` (stops status nagging about the old link)\n   - `retry_verify \"$newgid\" \"url:$newurl\"` — new link confirmed alive (`retry running`/`already on disk`) or diagnosed (`real problem`, marked permanent, rc 1)\n   - `ensure_healer` + `--tmux`\n4. **Robustness fix**: `retry_verify` currently references `$quiet` which only exists in `cmd_retry`'s scope — change to `${quiet:-0}` so `replace` can reuse it under `set -u`.\n5. **Surface**: usage() command + example lines (lines 49–95), `# POS_SUBCMDS:` header (line 4) gains `replace`.\n\n### Tests (stub harness `/tmp/opencode/dl-test`)\n\nNew `== replace ==` section (placed so `download.retry` already holds `url:…/part.iso` from the existing 404 test) plus advisory checks in `status`:\n\n- **status advisory** — `status` contains `needs fresh link: part.iso` while the old link is still marked\n- **replace success** — new URL in curl log with `\"dir\":\"/tmp/dl\"` + `\"out\":\"part.iso\"`, message `replaced eeeeeeeeeeeeeeee → …`, old id **gone** from `download.retry`, rc 0 (new gid completes instantly)\n- **replace dead new link** — `ADDURI_GID=dddd…` → rc 1, `real problem`, `url:https://new.example/…` now permanent\n- **replace torrent** (`cccc…`) → rc 1 with torrent hint\n- **replace active** (unknown full gid → default `active` fixture) → rc 1\n- **replace missing args** → rc 1\n- **replace via prefix** (`eeeeee`) → resolves\n- Existing 119 tests must stay green (advisory lines are additive; all checks are substring-based)\n\n### Docs & regen\n\n- `DOC/POS.md` — `replace` row + one sentence in the outage-resilience paragraph\n- `DOC/howto/network.md` — outage recipe gains the \"dead link → `status` says so → `replace <gid> <new-url>` resumes it\" step\n- `AGENT_TODO.md` — **Done** entry (2026-08-12)\n- `make gen` (completions/AGENT_Context dispatch) → `make check`\n- Verify: full stub suite green, `bash -n`\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. **Command name** — I recommend **`replace <gid> <url>`**. Alternatives: `relink` (shorter, but reads like symlinks), `refresh <gid> <url>`. OK with `replace`?\n2. **Scope of the advisory** — `status` only (as you asked), or also mark those rows in `list`'s STOPPED table (e.g. append `⚠`)? I'd keep it `status`-only for now — smaller surface.\n\nIf those choices are fine, I'll implement, run the full suite + `make gen && make check`, and report back for the commit.",
