MD/MIG_RULE:\n```bash\nsched_parse_legacy_rule() {  # \"$1\" = legacy line → sets MIG_MSG MIG_CMD MIG_RULE\n    local line=\"$1\" cond=\"\" msg=\"\" s=\"$1\" parts=\"\" m\n    while [[ \"$s\" == *\" if \"* ]]; do\n        m=\"${s%% if *}\"\n        s=\"${s#*\" if \"}\"\n        if [[ \"$s\" == *\" if \"* ]]; then parts+=\"${m} if \"; else parts+=\"${m}\"; fi\n    done\n    msg=\"$parts\"; cond=\"$s\"\n    [ -n \"$cond\" ] || return 1\n    local -a tokens=()\n    read -r -a tokens <<< \"$cond\"\n    local n=${#tokens[@]}\n    [ \"$n\" -ge 2 ] || return 1\n    for ((i=n-2; i>=0; i--)); do\n        case \"${tokens[i]}\" in\n            \">=\"|\"<=\"|\"==\"|\"!=\"|\">\"|\"<\")\n                if sched_numeric \"${tokens[i+1]}\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n                    MIG_OP=\"${tokens[i]}\"; MIG_THRESH=\"${tokens[i+1]}\"\n                    if [ \"$i\" -eq 0 ]; then MIG_CMD=\"${tokens[0]}\"\n                    else\n                        MIG_CMD=\"$(printf '%s ' \"${tokens[@]:0:i}\")\"; MIG_CMD=\"${MIG_CMD% }\"\n                    fi\n                    MIG_MSG=\"$(sched_strip_quotes \"$msg\")\"\n                    MIG_RULE=\"$MIG_OP $MIG_THRESH\"\n                    return 0\n                fi ;;\n        esac\n    done\n    return 1\n}\n```\nThis is exactly eventer_parse_rule with RULE split out. \n\nNote the old eventer semantics: `\"msg\" if cmd op thresh`. MSG unquoted. Good.\n\n### The tool\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n# POS: system schedule — Scheduled jobs: run a command on a timer; notify on threshold/change/error/always or silently\n# POS_SUBCMDS: run list config enable disable status migrate\n# POS_FLAGS: --dry-run\n\nsource \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../lib/common.sh\" 2>/dev/null || source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/common.sh\"\nsource \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../lib/scheduler-lib.sh\" 2>/dev/null || source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/scheduler-lib.sh\"\nsource \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../lib/notify.sh\" 2>/dev/null || source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/notify.