          "text": "Done — committed as `d4d38ad` (`feat: pos system backup copies to USB after verification — sha256-proven 100%`), pre-commit `make check` green, working tree clean except `dream.md`.\n\n## What `pos system backup` now does\n\n**After** the archive finishes and verifies (exactly what you asked — detection is post-backup, so a stick plugged in while tar+gpg ran is found):\n\n1. **Detect** — mounted removable storage via `lsblk -J` + a recursive `jq` filter (rm==true, mounted, type part|disk). Space-y mountpoints like `/media/you/My Stick` are safe (JSON parsing). No detection, no prompt: pin your stick with `BACKUP_USB_ROOT=/mnt/usb` in `system.env` (also what cron use-cases want).\n2. **Ask** — none mounted → one chance to plug one in: `Plug a USB drive in now and press Enter to re-check (or 's' to skip)`. One stick → `Copy backup to /media/you/STICK/backups/? [y/N]`. Several → numbered pick (`0` = skip). `n` or EOF (cron) skips silently, rc stays 0.\n3. **Copy** — to `<usb>/backups/` (created if missing). `chmod 600` is best-effort — a vfat stick that ignores chmod warns, never fails the copy.\n4. **Check 100%** — `sha256sum` of source vs copy compared before any success is announced: match → `OK Transfer verified 100% (sha256 match)` + notify; mismatch → both hashes printed, `notify_send \"USB copy FAILED…\"`, rc=1. The ERR trap is re-armed before this phase so a USB failure no longer notifies the misleading \"Backup FAILED\".\n\n## Verified\n- Stub harness `/tmp/opencode/backup-test/` (HOME-isolated, sudo/gpg/lsblk/telegram stubs, corrupting-`cp` and vfat-`chmod` override stubs, per-test lsblk JSON fixtures): **40/40 green** — skip (s / cron-EOF), seam y/n, auto-detect single, multi pick 2 & 0, re-scan after replug, corrupt copy → rc=1 + honest notify, vfat tolerance.\n- `make check` OK (also as pre-commit hook); dispatcher `pos system backup --help` works.\n\n## Docs updated\n`usage()` Environment, `DOC/POS.md` backup row, `DOC/howto/system.md` 