          "text": "## Plan: `usb-automount` feature (integrated like `autostart`)\n\n### Goal\nA `features/usb-automount.sh` feature + flag-gated `systemd/usb-automount.service`, wired exactly like the `autostart` pattern. When a USB stick is plugged in (or at boot for sticks already in), it auto-mounts at `/media/<label>` **world-writable** (`-o umask=000`), so `pos system backup`'s post-backup USB detection finds it and the user's copy succeeds. No `pos` tool — features stay bare scripts.\n\n### New files\n\n**1. `features/usb-automount.sh`** (~90 lines, `set -euo pipefail`, per `templates/feature.sh`)\n- Root guard: `[ \"$(id -u)\" -eq 0 ] || exec sudo \"$0\" \"$@\"` (service runs as root; manual run self-elevates). Test-only env seam `AUTOMOUNT_SKIP_ROOT_GUARD=1` to bypass.\n- **udev self-install** (first root run, idempotent): write `/etc/udev/rules.d/99-usb-automount.rules`:\n  ```\n  ACTION==\"add\", KERNEL==\"sd[a-z]*\", SUBSYSTEM==\"block\", ENV{ID_BUS}==\"usb\", TAG+=\"systemd\", SYSTEMD_WANTS=\"usb-automount.service\"\n  ```\n  then `udevadm control --reload` + `udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=block` (seams `UDEV_RULES_DIR`, `UDEVADM`). Rewrite only if content differs.\n- **Mount scan** (`lsblk -J -o NAME,PATH,LABEL,MOUNTPOINT,RM,TYPE` + recursive `jq` filter — same JSON technique as the backup tool): select `rm==true && type==\"part\"` (and whole-disk `type==\"disk\"` with no children) where `mountpoint==null`; skip already-mounted; skip `/boot/efi`-style fixed media (non-USB filtered by the udev rule anyway, but the scan re-checks `ID_BUS` isn't available via lsblk — use a second `lsblk -J` pass? No — the **boot** run should mount USB only; use `udevadm info`? Simplest: try `mount`, and for the scan accept all removable; the udev rule already restricts to USB for hotplug, boot run uses all removable — note in docs that the script mounts removable storage). Actually: filter to `rm==true` only; that's removable by definition. Good enough and documentable.\n- **Mount**: `mkdir -p /media/<label>` (dedupe with `-2`, `-3` on collision); try `mount -o umask=000 <dev> <mp>`; on failure retry plain `mount <dev> <mp>` (ext4/other). Dependency guards: `command -v lsblk jq mount`.\n- Log to `${HOME:-/root}/.usb-automount.log` (autostart precedent), `-h|--help` via `usage()`.\n\n**2. `systemd/usb-automount.service`** (~12 lines, autostart.service shape)\n```\n[Unit]\nDescription=Auto-mount USB storage (features/usb-automount.sh)\nAfter=local-fs.target\n[Service]\nType=oneshot\nExecStart=/usr/local/bin/usb-automount.sh\n[Install]\nWantedBy=multi-user.target\n```\n`Type=oneshot` (hotplug trigger = one scan each, like the health digest pattern); enabled only when the flag is green.\n\n### Modified files\n- **`postinstall.sh`** — one gate line in the systemd loop mirroring autostart (line ~146):\n  ```bash\n  if [ \"$svc_name\" = \"usb-automount.service\" ] && ! flag_is_set usb-automount; then\n      warn \"usb-automount feature not installed — skipping usb-automount.service (run ./install.sh --feature)\"\n      continue\n  fi\n  ```\n- **`DOC/SYSTEMD.md`** — `usb-automount.service` section (purpose, unit, udev rule, log path, world-writable note) + gating code block gains the second unit.\n- **`DOC/SCRIPTS.md`** — new `## features/usb-automount.sh — USB automount feature` section (autostart style: file, purpose, how it works, config/log) + update the systemd-services bullet (line ~111) and TOC (line 15).\n- **`DOC/AGENT_Context_Project.md`** — hand-edit: §2 tree `features/` block gains `usb-automount.sh` line; hand-maintained filetable row above the GEN marker gains `features/usb-automount.sh | <n> | USB automount (udev + systemd, flag-gated) |`. `make gen` refreshes the docmap/line ranges afterwards.\n- **`DOC/README.md`** — index rows for SCRIPTS.md/SYSTEMD.md feature mention (minor, only if the index lists autostart by name).\n- **`AGENT_TODO.md`** — Done entry in the commit.\n- No changes to `install.sh` (features auto-discovered), `bin/pos`, `preinstall.sh` (lsblk/jq/mount all in util-linux/jq — jq already in PACKAGES), no new `udev/` dir (per your choice).\n\n### Testing (`/tmp/opencode/usb-automount-test/`, throwaway per DEV.md §7)\nStub `sudo` (exec), `mount` (log args + optionally fail on `$MOUNT_FAIL_GLOB`), `udevadm` (log), `lsblk` (JSON fixtures via `LSBLK_JSON`), real `jq`. HOME-isolated, `AUTOMOUNT_SKIP_ROOT_GUARD=1`, `UDEV_RULES_DIR`/`UDEVADM` seams to temp. Cases (~12): mounts unmounted vfat label at `/media/<label>` with umask=000; skips already-mounted; whole-disk removable; multiple devices incl. label dedupe (`-2`); umask→plain fallback; second run idempotent no-op; udev rule written once (no rewrite when identical) + `udevadm` reload/trigger called; non-root run self-elevates via sudo stub; `-h` exit 0; log lines appended. Assert on stub logs + mountpoint markers.\n\n### Verification\n`bash -n features/usb-automount.sh && bash -n postinstall.sh`, harness green, `make gen && make check`, then commit (`feat: usb-automount feature — udev+systemd auto-mount of USB sticks, flag-gated like autostart`), leaving `dream.md` untracked.\n\nOne thing I'll decide during implementation (noted for your awareness): the boot scan mounts **all removable** block devices (the udev rule restricts hotplug to USB via `ID_BUS==usb`; `lsblk` can't easily filter USB-only). If that distinction matters to you, say so and I'll add an `ID_BUS` check via `udevadm info` per device.\n\nReady to build on approval.",
