          "type": "text",
          "text": "Done — committed as `a3c01a0` (8 files, +217/−19, pre-commit `make check` green).\n\n## What was built\n\n**`features/usb-automount.sh`** (134 lines, `./install.sh --feature` → `/usr/local/bin/usb-automount.sh`, flag `usb-automount`)\n- Root guard: self-re-execs via `sudo` when run by a user (service runs as root).\n- First root run self-installs the hotplug udev rule `99-usb-automount.rules` (`SYSTEMD_WANTS=\"usb-automount.service\"`) + `udevadm control --reload` + block trigger — install-only-if-missing, so a user-edited rule is never clobbered.\n- Scans `lsblk -J` (same recursive-jq technique as the backup tool) for unmounted removable partitions and raw whole-disk filesystems; mounts each at `/media/<label>` with `-o umask=000` (world-writable → your user can write, which is what makes the backup USB-copy flow work), plain-mount fallback for filesystems that reject `umask`, `-2`/`-3` bump on label collisions, `usb-<name>` when unlabeled. Idempotent; logs to `${HOME:-/root}/.usb-automount.log`.\n\n**`systemd/usb-automount.service`** — `Type=oneshot`, `WantedBy=multi-user.target`: boot + hotplug + manual `systemctl start usb-automount` all do one scan.\n\n**`postinstall.sh`** — one gate line in the systemd loop mirroring autostart exactly (`flag_is_set usb-automount` → skip with hint).\n\n**Docs** — SYSTEMD.md (service section + gating block), SCRIPTS.md (feature section + bullet + TOC), AGENT_Context (tree + filetable; also corrected a stale `postinstall.sh` count 152→163), README index, AGENT_TODO Done entry.\n\n## Verification\n- Stub suite `/tmp/opencode/usb-automount-test` — **47/47 green**: mount/no-op/skip/fallback/failure paths, dedupe, raw disk, no-label, udev install-once + preserve-edits, root-guard re-exec, lsblk failure, help, empty scan.\n- `make gen && make check` green; `bash -n` clean; exec bit set per repo convention.\n\n## Two things worth knowing\n1. **Bash gotcha found:** `\"${VAR:-{...}}\"` (a `{` inside a parameter-expansion default) mis-parses — it appended a stray `}`. Recorded in the AGENT_TODO entry; my script avoids the pattern. Flag it if you want it added to DEV.md §7.\n2. **Scope note:** the udev rule restricts hotplug to USB (`ID_BUS==\"usb\"`); the boot scan covers *all* removable media (as planned — `lsblk` can't filter USB-only easily).\n\nTree is clean except `dream.md`, still untracked per your earlier choice. Nothing pushed (as usual, say the word if you want that).",
