          "text": "That output is exactly the problem to fix. Diagnosing it: `pos entertainment config` bare-mode is a **wall of text** (file cat + key dump), `set` is manual `KEY=VALUE` typing, and even `pos config entertainment`'s editor treats `ENABLED` as free-text CSV you hand-edit (`weather, 5m gold, 1h`) and unknown keys as a late warning. The registry already knows scopes, keys, flags, and dynamic plugin keys (`*plugins`) — what's missing is **value semantics** (types/options per key) and a **modern UI layer** so the editor can render the right control for each key and assemble values for you.\n\nYes — everything should be dynamic, interactive, and straightforward. Here's the plan.\n\n## Plan: Interactive everything — generic guided config editor + `pos menu`\n\n### The core idea\nOne **declarative, typed config editor** replaces every raw config screen. Keys declare their *kind* (enum/bool/list/secret/plain) and the UI renders the matching control — and for plugin-derived keys (`ENABLED`), the options are built live from the installed plugins. Same registry, same env files, one code path.\n\n### Step 1 — `lib/ui.sh` (new): modern prompt helpers, gum-backed\n- `ui_choose` / `ui_multiselect` / `ui_input [secret]` / `ui_confirm` — gum (`gum choose --multi`, `gum input --password`, `gum confirm`, `gum style`) with **pure-bash fallback** (numbered list / `read -rp`) when gum is missing, stdin isn't a TTY, or `POS_UI=plain` (the test seam — DEV.md §7 registry, `auto|gum|plain`).\n- This is your \"modern UI on CLI\": styled headers, live choosers — but it degrades gracefully for cron/systemd/tests, so nothing breaks on a minimal box.\n- `preinstall.sh`: curl-install the gum binary from GitHub releases (same pattern as yt-dlp — gum isn't in Debian repos). Auto-installed by default = modern UI out of the box.\n\n### Step 2 — `lib/config-ui.sh` upgrade: typed keys + dynamic options\n- Extend the `# POS_CONFIG:` flags field with new tokens alongside the existing `secret|digits|num|float`:\n  - `enum(a|b|c)` → `ui_choose`; `bool` → `ui_confirm`; `list` → `ui_multiselect`; `secret` → masked input; numbers → validated input.\n  - `*plugins` (already supported) means \"build `list` options from the installed plugins' `# POS_KEYS:` headers\" — this is what makes `ENABLED` dynamic.\n- `cfg_ui` re-renders with `ui.sh`: current values as a menu; edit control per type; Enter keeps / `-` clears preserved; non-TTY falls back to the current numbered flow.\n\n### Step 3 — flagship: `pos entertainment config` becomes a guided wizard\n- **Bare invocation on a TTY → wizard** (the wall of text moves behind `--show`; non-TTY keeps current show behavior).\n- `ENABLED` = multiselect of *installed plugins*, each with an interval picker → the CSV is assembled for you (kills the `weather, daily gold, daily` hand-edit).\n- `WEATHER_LAT/LON` validated number inputs with current values as defaults; city free text; `secret` masked.\n- **Undeclared-key headache → interactive choice**: keep / edit / remove, instead of \"saving anyway\".\n\n### Step 4 — `pos menu`: full-tree interactive navigator (the \"everything\" umbrella)\n- Category-less tool (like `pos config`/`pos tree`), added to `INTERACTIVE_CMDS`.\n- Category → tool → **[run guided / run bare / help / back]**. Guided mode prompts per `# POS_FLAGS:` flag (`--no-*`/bare = `ui_confirm`, others = `ui_input`) then runs the tool; `--dry-run` prints the assembled command (test seam + DEV.md doctrine).\n\n### Step 5 — retrofit seed (first batch, sets the convention)\nBare invocation prompts instead of erroring on: `pos network scan` (CIDR), `pos media mp3`/`mp4` (URL), `pos docker compose` (action/service), `pos share smb client mount` (share). Rest of the 33 later.\n\n### Step 6 — verification + docs\n- Harnesses in `/tmp/opencode/`: `ui-test` (each type's control via `POS_UI=plain` + PTY driving via `script`), `menu-test` (guided command assembly, dry-run), wizard test for entertainment (fake plugin fixtures with `# POS_KEYS:` markers).\n- Docs: POS.md (menu + config rows), SCRIPTS.md (ui.sh), DEV.md (typed-config convention, `POS_UI` seam, gum-fallback doctrine), AGENT_Context (files + filetable rows + \"How to modify\"), AGENT_TODO. `make gen && make check`.\n\n### Scope/decisions I'm making (say so if you disagree)\n- **gum** is the \"modern UI\" engine (single static binary, exactly the Charm/CLI-modern style), with the pure-bash fallback so nothing depends on it.\n- gum **auto-installed** in preinstall (like yt-dlp) — not optional-by-default.\n- The old flat text menu stays reachable via the non-TTY fallback (and `POS_UI=plain`), so nothing regresses.\n- Core is Steps 1–3; Step 4 is the broad win; Step 5 seeds the convention (not all 33 tools at once).\n\nReady to build on approval.",
