          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Now `bin/pos-entertainment-config` — the flagship wizard. Rewrite the bare-mode (non-set, non-help) branch:\n- `--show` → show (wall of text, current behavior)\n- bare + TTY → wizard\n- bare + non-TTY → show (keep current behavior)\n\nWizard flow:\n1. ui_header \"entertainment config\"\n2. Config file path + current ENABLED summary\n3. config_wizard_enabled (ENABLED multiselect + intervals)\n4. Plugin-declared keys loop: confirm \"Set KEY? (current...)\" → ui_input w/ default; WEATHER_LAT/LON → float-validated; write via write_config_key\n5. Undeclared key cleanup: keys in file not in ENABLED/plugin-declared → confirm remove → remove_config_key\n\nAlso update usage() to document the wizard + --show.\n\nThe tool sources common.sh + entertainment-lib.sh. The wizard uses _ent_source_ui (available from ent-lib).\n\nFor numeric validation of WEATHER_LAT/LON in the wizard: use ui_validate_num? That's in ui.sh (needs sourcing — done via _ent_source_ui). `ui_validate_num float \"WEATHER_LAT (desc)\" \"$cur\"` → returns validated value. \n\nWizard code:\n\n```bash\nwizard() {\n    _ent_source_ui || return 1\n    local d line plugin key desc req cur val\n    d=\"$(plugin_dir)\"\n\n    ui_header \"entertainment config\"\n    echo \"  Config: $CONFIG_FILE\" >&2\n    echo \"  ENABLED: $(config_value ENABLED)\" >&2\n\n    # 1. Auto-trigger list (multiselect + intervals)\n    config_wizard_enabled\n\n    # 2. Plugin-declared keys (WEATHER_* etc.)\n    while IFS= read -r line; do\n        [ -n \"$line\" ] || continue\n        IFS='|' read -r plugin key desc req <<<\"$line\"\n        cur=\"$(config_value \"$key\")\"\n        if ui_confirm \"${key} — ${desc}${cur:+ (current: ${cur})} — set it?\" \"${req:-n}\"; then\n            case \"$key\" in\n                WEATHER_LAT|WEATHER_LON)\n                    val=\"$(ui_validate_num float \"$key (latitude/longitude, e.g. 36.51)\" \"$cur\")\" || { warn \"aborted — $key unchanged\"; continue; }\n                    ;;\n                *)\n                    val=\"$(ui_input \"$key ($desc)\" \"$cur\")\" || { warn \"aborted — $key unchanged\"; continue; }\n                    ;;\n            esac\n            [ -z \"$val\" ] && continue\n            [ \"$val\" = \"$cur\" ] && continue\n            if [ \"$val\" = \"-\" ]; then\n                remove_config_key \"$key\"\n                log \"cleared $key\"\n            else\n                write_config_key \"$key\" \"$val\"\n                ok \"$key = $val saved\"\n            fi\n        fi\n    done <<< \"$(config_keys \"$d\")\"\n\n    # 3. Keys in the file that no installed plugin declares\n    local -A declared=()\n    declared[ENABLED]=1\n    while IFS= read -r line; do\n        IFS='|' read -r _plugin key _d _r <<<\"$line\"\n        [ -n \"$key\" ] && declared[$key]=1\n    done <<< \"$(config_keys \"$d\")\"\n    local k\n    if [ -f \"$CONFIG_FILE\" ]; then\n        while IFS='=' read -r k _v; do\n            [ -n \"$k\" ] || continue\n            case \"$k\" in \\#*) continue ;; esac\n            [ -n \"${declared[$k]:-}\" ] && continue\n            cur=\"$(config_value \"$k\")\"\n            if ui_confirm \"'$k' is not declared by any installed plugin (value: ${cur:-empty}) — remove it?\" y; then\n                remove_config_key \"$k\"\n                log \"removed $k\"\n            fi\n        done < <(grep -E '^[A-Z_]+=' \"$CONFIG_FILE\" || true)\n    fi\n\n    echo \"Entertainment config done.\" >&2\n}\n```\n\nHmm — step 2's `continue` inside the loop... `val=\"$(ui_validate_num ...)\" || { warn ...; continue; }` — `continue` inside `{ ...; }` inside an if-while loop — valid bash (continue applies to enclosing while). OK.\n\nWait — `ui_confirm \"${key} — ${desc}...\"` — desc contains e.g. \"latitude (required)\". Prompt is long but fine.\n\nIssue: WEATHER_LAT desc says required. For required keys default y — `\"${req:-n}\"` — req = \"required\" → y; \"optional\" → n; \"\" → n. \n\nAlso for secret plugin keys? None currently. Fine.\n\nNote the `case \"$key\" in WEATHER_LAT|WEATHER_LON)` — hardcoded knowledge. Slight smell but documented as \"well-known numeric keys\" — YAGNI-compliant (2 lines). Add comment.\n\nNow usage() update:\n\n```\nUsage: pos entertainment config [set KEY=VALUE ...]\n\nShow or edit the entertainment config. Bare invocation on a terminal opens\nthe interactive wizard (auto-trigger list via multiselect, plugin keys with\ncurrent values as defaults, undeclared-key cleanup); --show prints the raw\nconfig; 'set' sets one or more keys non-interactively.\n\nConfig file: $CONFIG_FILE\n\nKeys (declared by the installed plugins' # POS_KEYS: headers):\n$(keys_section \"$(plugin_dir)\")\n\nIntervals: ...\n\nExamples:\n  pos entertainment config              # interactive wizard\n  pos entertainment config --show       # raw config + key reference\n  pos entertainment config set ENABLED=\"weather, 5m gold, 1h\"\n  ...\n```\n\nAnd the main case:\n```bash\ncase \"${1:-}\" in\n    -h|--help) usage ;;\n    --show) show ;;\n    set) ... (unchanged) ;;\n    *)\n        if [ -t 0 ]; then\n            wizard\n        else\n            show\n        fi\n        ;;\nesac\n```\n\nExtract the current bare branch body into `show()`.\n\nNow write the edits to pos-entertainment-config.",
