fi` — keep the prompting branch *before* the `usage` guard and the dispatch `case`, and (when the prompt needs re-exec or arg assembly) define the helper function *before* its call site.\n\n### Testing\n\nLogic tests run in `POS_UI=plain` (deterministic, no gum). The gum path is a smoke test: a `POS_GUM` stub (fake `gum` binary that echoes its last argument) driven through a PTY — `printf 'answer\\n' | script -qec \"cmd\" /dev/null` (see [Interactive prompts](#testing-tools-that-need-root--systemd--missing-deps)). Assert **side effects** (env file writes, assembled commands), not keystrokes. Precedents: `lib/ui.sh` itself, `pos menu` (`bin/pos-menu`, `--dry-run` prints the assembled command), the entertainment wizard (`pos entertainment config` on a TTY), and the retrofit prompts in `pos-{network-scan,media-mp3,media-mp4,docker-compose,share-smb-client}`.\n\n---\n\n## Best Practices",
