                "patch": "Index: /mnt/hdd/ciya_space/work/repo/Linux_post_install/DOC/SCRIPTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /mnt/hdd/ciya_space/work/repo/Linux_post_install/DOC/SCRIPTS.md\n+++ /mnt/hdd/ciya_space/work/repo/Linux_post_install/DOC/SCRIPTS.md\n@@ -200,8 +200,27 @@\n Sourced by `bin/pos-entertainment-send|config|enable|disable|status` (after `lib/common.sh`). **Plugins must not source it** — their stdout is the sent message.\n \n ---\n \n+## lib/ui.sh — interactive UI layer\n+\n+**File:** `lib/ui.sh` (installed to `/usr/local/bin/ui.sh`)\n+**Purpose:** the repo's single interactive-input layer — menus, multi-select, text/secret input, confirm, headers — for the `pos` tools (`pos config`, `pos entertainment config` wizard, `pos menu`, and the bare-on-TTY prompts). See [DEV.md → Interactive UI Convention](DEV.md#interactive-ui-convention).\n+\n+Backend seam `POS_UI=auto|gum|plain` (auto = gum when `command -v gum` **and** stdin is a TTY, else plain; `POS_GUM` overrides the gum path for tests). Both backends render prompts to **stderr** and print the chosen result to **stdout**:\n+\n+```bash\n+source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../lib/ui.sh\" 2>/dev/null || source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/ui.sh\"\n+target=\"$(ui_input \"Target network (e.g. 192.168.1.0/24)\" \"\")\" || exit 1   # user aborted\n+pick=\"$(ui_choose \"Action\" run install list)\"                              # → \"install\"\n+many=\"$(ui_multiselect \"Plugins\" weather joke gold)\"                       # → \"weather,gold\"\n+ui_confirm \"Really?\"                                                       # 0 = yes, 1 = no\n+```\n+\n+`ui_typed` dispatches on a type token: `bool→confirm`, `enum(a,b,c)→choose`, `list→multiselect`, `secret→masked`, `digits|num|float→validated`, else text. Keys: Enter=keep/confirm, `-`=clear, `q`=quit/abort.\n+\n+---\n+\n ## features/autostart.sh — boot-time feature\n \n **File:** `features/autostart.sh` (installed to `/usr/local/bin/autostart.sh` by `./install.sh --feature`)\n **Purpose:** runs once at boot via `autostart.service` (only when the `autostart` flag is green) and logs basic connectivity status.\n",
